From 9d89cc41629fdd048564834755b440a8158d17f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:49:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 375/381] Part: --export-web writes a 3D view to turn in a
 browser, one HTML without libraries

FreeCAD's WebGL export loads three.js from the internet: not without the
net and not always on a phone. PartWebView.export (from fcx.web of the
room models) writes WebGL 1 with the data in the page: the visible
objects in their colours, curved faces shaded smoothly (the normals of
tessellate), edges, a switch for each group or part, light or dark,
walls in front taken away, two fingers on a phone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
